{"diagnosis": "Fetch makes no progress (max_addr 0x00000000, FAIL 0xdead after 2009 cycles). In mem_state 0 mem_valid is assigned mem_la_use_prefetched_high_word instead of its complement, so normal fetches never assert mem_valid while prefetched-high-word hits spuriously request. The state-1 assert mem_valid == !mem_la_use_prefetched_high_word confirms the inversion, explaining the stall.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picorv32.v b/picorv32.v
--- a/picorv32.v
+++ b/picorv32.v
@@ -582,6 +582,6 @@
 				0: begin
 					if (mem_do_prefetch || mem_do_rinst || mem_do_rdata) begin
-						mem_valid <= mem_la_use_prefetched_high_word;
+						mem_valid <= !mem_la_use_prefetched_high_word;
 						mem_instr <= mem_do_prefetch || mem_do_rinst;
 						mem_wstrb <= 0;
 						mem_state <= 1;
", "expected": "tohost PASS (not FAIL 0xdead) with fetch progress max_addr>0x00000000 and checksum != 563b7c10626ff25de2b3c430956c7c113e448c4efaea068f9b83a198d4322b15"}

